WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.230
<b>Nakatomi Yoka</b>

00:00.550 --> 00:03.230
Okay, why don't you introduce yourself?

00:05.740 --> 00:07.190
Whoops, I forgot.

00:08.410 --> 00:09.620
Ah, sorry!

00:09.620 --> 00:10.590
I'm sorry.

00:10.590 --> 00:12.540
Does it hurt that much?

00:12.540 --> 00:13.760
Sorry, sorry.

00:13.760 --> 00:14.350
Are you okay?

00:14.690 --> 00:15.670
Can you stand?

00:15.670 --> 00:16.410
Try standing up.

00:18.320 --> 00:19.890
Huh.

00:19.890 --> 00:22.500
So that's what your face 
looks like, Nakatomi-san.

00:23.080 --> 00:24.710
Be nice, Shizuru-chan.

00:24.710 --> 00:26.190
Hey, I'm Reimi.

00:26.190 --> 00:28.260
Feel free to call me Reimi.

00:28.260 --> 00:29.360
Wait, that's the same.

00:29.360 --> 00:31.370
Your full name is Flunking Reimi.

00:31.370 --> 00:32.470
No, it isn't!

00:32.470 --> 00:34.350
Sorry to frighten you, Nakatomi-san.

00:34.580 --> 00:36.030
There's nothing to be scared of.

00:36.030 --> 00:37.090
We won't bite.

00:54.320 --> 00:58.070
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

02:15.500 --> 02:18.520
Are you all residents of Higashi-Agano?

02:15.530 --> 02:20.860
Episode 3       Short, Happy, and Easy

02:18.520 --> 02:19.630
Yes, we are.

02:19.630 --> 02:21.140
Is this a train?

02:21.140 --> 02:22.360
Yes, that's right.

02:22.360 --> 02:24.310
It's been so long since I've seen one.

02:24.310 --> 02:26.700
Where, pray tell, are you from?

02:27.130 --> 02:28.530
Agano, one stop over.

02:28.530 --> 02:29.570
Agano?

02:28.860 --> 02:30.060
Agano, she says.

02:29.410 --> 02:30.410
Agano...

02:30.410 --> 02:31.920
Agano, huh?

02:32.370 --> 02:33.780
My goodness.

02:33.780 --> 02:35.950
That's quite the journey nowadays.

02:35.950 --> 02:37.710
I imagine it was harrowing.

02:37.710 --> 02:39.460
Yeah, I guess.

02:39.460 --> 02:41.510
Is everyone in Agano faring well?

02:42.230 --> 02:44.950
I suppose you could say that.

02:44.950 --> 02:49.810
Please, feel free to cultivate—
I mean, recuperate here for the time being.

02:49.810 --> 02:54.070
Fortunately, Higashi-Agano's 
dwindling population

02:54.070 --> 02:55.920
means we have plenty of housing to spare.

02:55.920 --> 02:57.360
Whoa, we'd love to!

02:57.360 --> 02:57.980
By all means.

02:57.980 --> 02:58.720
Yes.

02:58.220 --> 02:59.240
Great idea.

02:59.240 --> 03:02.450
I'm afraid we don't have much money.

03:02.450 --> 03:04.450
Oh, that won't be a problem.

03:04.450 --> 03:05.360
Yay!

03:05.360 --> 03:07.060
Thank you very much.

03:10.990 --> 03:12.420
Good evening.

03:12.790 --> 03:14.420
Good evening.

03:14.700 --> 03:16.760
Everyone here is so friendly.

03:16.760 --> 03:18.240
It's nothing like Agano.

03:18.240 --> 03:19.990
Back home, it's carnivores 
versus herbivores,

03:19.990 --> 03:21.980
and they even had to cancel 
the summer festival.

03:21.980 --> 03:25.510
Yeah, over what the 
shrine offerings should be.

03:25.510 --> 03:27.730
I was, like, who cares?

03:27.730 --> 03:32.300
Should've just gone with the Agano specialties:
rice, bitter melon, and barleywheat.

03:32.300 --> 03:33.760
Bitter melon?

03:33.760 --> 03:34.460
Huh?

03:34.460 --> 03:37.560
Matsuta-san, do you hate bitter melon?

03:37.560 --> 03:38.940
Ah, no!

03:38.940 --> 03:41.230
I wouldn't go that far.

03:41.230 --> 03:43.180
It's totally uncute.

03:43.180 --> 03:47.180
Bitter melon just feels a lot more rustic 
than zucchini or bell peppers.

03:47.180 --> 03:48.650
I think it's good.

03:48.650 --> 03:50.820
Typical Akira.

03:50.820 --> 03:52.950
Will we really be okay?

03:52.950 --> 03:55.040
In a big city like Ikebukuro, that is.

03:55.040 --> 03:57.820
We have no idea if it's still like that now.

03:57.110 --> 04:00.410
Matsuta-san, have you 
ever been to Ikebukuro?

04:00.830 --> 04:04.670
I used to live there, 
but I moved back to Higashi-Agano.

04:04.670 --> 04:05.610
I'm so jealous!

04:05.610 --> 04:06.500
What was it like?

04:06.500 --> 04:08.160
It's more urban than this place, right?

04:08.160 --> 04:09.280
Let me think.

04:09.280 --> 04:10.610
I believe it was.

04:10.610 --> 04:11.960
You believe?

04:11.960 --> 04:13.210
My apologies.

04:13.210 --> 04:15.300
It's no longer of any concern to me.

04:15.560 --> 04:18.030
Have you seen this girl before?

04:18.030 --> 04:19.650
Near Ikebukuro.

04:19.650 --> 04:20.470
I can't say.

04:20.470 --> 04:22.690
I guess that's only natural.

04:26.560 --> 04:28.360
There, I'm done.

04:28.360 --> 04:30.050
Do these bangs look okay?

04:30.050 --> 04:30.990
Yeah, yeah.

04:30.990 --> 04:33.110
C'mon, look a little closer.

04:33.110 --> 04:34.970
I'm fine with them if you are.

04:35.780 --> 04:36.670
Let's take a photo!

04:36.930 --> 04:38.380
To celebrate my new bangs.

04:43.810 --> 04:45.190
Shizuru-chan.

04:45.190 --> 04:46.440
What are you doing?

04:46.440 --> 04:47.800
Hurry up.

04:48.800 --> 04:50.960
Huh! Not too shabby!

04:50.960 --> 04:51.770
Reimi-chan!

04:51.770 --> 04:53.080
Why, yes.

04:53.080 --> 04:57.480
In Higashi-Agano, we believe 
in treating our guests with hospitality.

04:57.480 --> 05:00.040
I recommend our mist sauna in particular.

05:00.040 --> 05:01.410
Well, I say "recommend,"

05:01.410 --> 05:02.970
but you simply must.

05:02.970 --> 05:04.730
Please make sure you use it.

05:04.730 --> 05:05.810
Ah, sure.

05:06.120 --> 05:07.720
Till we meet again, then.

05:10.150 --> 05:12.480
Do we reek of sweat?

05:12.480 --> 05:14.280
Where is this sauna, anyway?

05:14.880 --> 05:15.870
There?

05:15.870 --> 05:17.830
Huh, looks fancy!

05:21.520 --> 05:23.790
Wow! Check out this mist!

05:23.790 --> 05:25.530
Nice! Let's go inside.

05:25.530 --> 05:27.450
You could totally detox here.

05:28.010 --> 05:29.210
I'll pass.

05:29.210 --> 05:30.230
Why?

05:30.230 --> 05:33.300
Akira-chan, let's take this chance 
to wash and dry our clothes.

05:33.300 --> 05:34.340
No, thanks.

05:34.340 --> 05:37.100
Maybe if I was alone, but I'm 
not going in with everyone.

05:37.100 --> 05:38.200
I get it.

05:38.200 --> 05:40.290
You're too shy to undress in front of us.

05:40.290 --> 05:41.970
There's nothing to be ashamed of.

05:41.970 --> 05:43.330
Anyway, I'm good.

05:45.730 --> 05:47.520
I wonder...

05:47.520 --> 05:50.440
Was it really the right move to leave Agano?

05:50.440 --> 05:53.440
There's no way I'd want to remain 
there alone, though.

06:10.440 --> 06:12.110
Pardon my intrusion.

06:12.400 --> 06:15.550
I thought you might be hungry 
after the sauna.

06:15.550 --> 06:18.010
Oh, thank you very much.

06:21.570 --> 06:22.800
Mushrooms...

06:22.800 --> 06:24.230
Do you not like them?

06:24.230 --> 06:25.120
Huh?

06:25.120 --> 06:26.850
Oh, no, I'm fine with them.

06:26.850 --> 06:28.300
I'm glad to hear it.

06:28.300 --> 06:30.430
This mixed rice is delicious.

06:30.430 --> 06:32.250
It's made with matsutake.

06:32.490 --> 06:34.940
Did you go in the mist sauna?

06:34.940 --> 06:37.230
Ah, yeah, technically.

06:37.230 --> 06:38.150
The others did.

06:38.150 --> 06:40.230
That's great to hear.

06:40.230 --> 06:42.840
Please, rest up plenty for the night.

06:42.840 --> 06:45.040
Take it nice and easy.

06:45.040 --> 06:45.860
Thanks.

06:54.370 --> 06:56.850
What's with all the food, Akira?

06:56.850 --> 06:58.160
What's going on?

06:58.160 --> 07:00.840
Matsuta-san brought this over earlier.

07:01.140 --> 07:02.830
They pulled out all the stops!

07:02.830 --> 07:05.380
That sauna session made me hungry.

07:05.380 --> 07:06.590
Let's dig in.

07:06.590 --> 07:08.080
I want this pork-wrapped enoki!

07:08.080 --> 07:09.120
Hang on!

07:09.480 --> 07:10.310
What?

07:10.310 --> 07:11.410
Don't you think it's weird?

07:11.410 --> 07:12.010
What's weird?

07:12.010 --> 07:12.980
The people here!

07:12.980 --> 07:14.100
Huh? You think?

07:14.100 --> 07:15.110
I think they're nice.

07:15.110 --> 07:16.450
Mushrooms on their heads aside.

07:16.450 --> 07:17.210
Yeah!

07:17.210 --> 07:18.500
What's the deal with those?!

07:18.500 --> 07:19.300
Wanna ask?

07:19.300 --> 07:21.130
You shouldn't do that.

07:21.130 --> 07:21.960
Huh? Why not?

07:21.960 --> 07:22.890
Oh, I know.

07:22.890 --> 07:25.920
It's like asking someone 
if they're wearing a wig.

07:25.920 --> 07:27.320
Etiquette. Manners.

07:27.320 --> 07:28.230
Oh, is that why?

07:28.230 --> 07:29.100
Not the point!

07:29.100 --> 07:31.170
What's the big deal if they have mushrooms?

07:31.170 --> 07:33.690
Everyone in Agano's an animal, you know.

07:33.690 --> 07:35.860
The folks here aren't obsessed with meat.

07:35.860 --> 07:36.900
They're friendly.

07:36.900 --> 07:38.830
Higashi-Agano's a nice place.

07:38.830 --> 07:40.430
So unconcerned...

07:56.110 --> 07:57.300
Reimi.

07:57.300 --> 07:58.850
Hey, Reimi.

07:59.850 --> 08:01.640
Flunking Reimi!

08:03.600 --> 08:05.880
Fine! I can go to the bathroom by myself!

08:11.770 --> 08:16.240
How come there's a huge sauna right there, 
but the bathroom's so far away?

08:16.240 --> 08:17.940
Who designed this place?

08:23.110 --> 08:24.630
Finally...

08:24.630 --> 08:26.110
Some new blood.

08:34.640 --> 08:37.600
Outsiders are so dumb.

08:37.600 --> 08:38.980
They don't suspect a thing.

08:38.980 --> 08:40.430
They just do everything we say.

08:40.430 --> 08:41.670
We'll get them in one fell swoop.

08:41.670 --> 08:43.440
The faster, the better.

08:43.440 --> 08:45.460
They'll be joining us soon.

08:46.460 --> 08:48.490
It's for their own good.

08:48.490 --> 08:50.380
We're doing them a favor.

08:54.000 --> 08:54.550
Who's there?!

09:12.500 --> 09:13.650
What's wrong?

09:17.020 --> 09:18.440
Shizuru-chan...

09:19.260 --> 09:21.110
I'm wide awake now.

09:21.110 --> 09:21.960
What happened?

09:30.270 --> 09:31.450
Matsuta-san?

09:31.780 --> 09:35.420
The unfamiliar surroundings 
must have given her a bad dream.

09:35.420 --> 09:37.330
Don't scare us like that.

09:37.330 --> 09:39.300
Akira, apologize to Matsuta-san.

09:39.570 --> 09:42.260
Say sorry for screaming and making a fuss.

09:42.260 --> 09:43.850
Think nothing of it.

09:43.850 --> 09:45.690
Have yourselves a good night.

09:47.010 --> 09:49.090
Let's go back to sleep.

09:49.090 --> 09:50.810
This place is scary.

09:50.810 --> 09:52.180
We gotta leave right away!

09:52.180 --> 09:53.540
You can't be serious.

09:53.540 --> 09:55.060
What a scaredy-cat.

09:55.060 --> 09:56.300
No!

09:56.300 --> 09:57.720
I'm not just crying wolf!

09:57.720 --> 09:59.770
Snuggle up with her, Reimi.

09:59.770 --> 10:00.520
No way.

10:00.520 --> 10:02.150
Akira turns in her sleep.

10:02.150 --> 10:04.060
Let's stop by the bathroom, Akira-chan.

10:04.060 --> 10:05.680
You still need to go, right?

10:05.680 --> 10:06.790
Yeah.

10:07.310 --> 10:08.620
Are you there?

10:08.620 --> 10:09.920
I'm right here.

10:09.920 --> 10:12.120
Don't you move, Nadeko-chan!

10:12.120 --> 10:13.500
Got it.

10:16.160 --> 10:18.020
Not a star in the sky.

10:18.380 --> 10:20.450
Is tomorrow another cloudy day?

10:24.180 --> 10:25.830
You're being tricked!

10:25.830 --> 10:27.230
Conspiracy nut, much?

10:27.230 --> 10:29.610
Akira sure loves that Freemanson stuff.

10:29.610 --> 10:30.810
Mason!

10:30.810 --> 10:32.060
It's okay.

10:32.060 --> 10:33.430
We'll be leaving soon.

10:36.360 --> 10:37.540
Yikes.

10:37.540 --> 10:38.830
All this in one night?

10:38.830 --> 10:40.370
Did it get too much sunlight?

10:40.370 --> 10:41.530
There's no way.

10:41.530 --> 10:42.710
It's been cloudy all this time.

10:42.710 --> 10:45.650
Also, this place is really damp 
compared to Agano.

10:45.650 --> 10:47.870
These vines have spread everywhere.

10:47.870 --> 10:49.240
Ah, they've fruited already.

10:53.180 --> 10:55.610
They say the bitter part 
is chock-full of nutrients.

10:56.170 --> 10:58.540
Why are you so stunned?

10:58.540 --> 10:59.910
Huh? Why?

10:59.910 --> 11:04.640
Direct sunlight does nothing 
but harm all living things!

11:04.640 --> 11:05.880
Heat! Desiccation!

11:05.880 --> 11:08.640
The laws of the universe dictate 
that you'll wilt and burn to a crisp!

11:08.640 --> 11:09.890
Huh...

11:09.890 --> 11:14.240
Growing heartily, flowering, and bearing fruit
in such conditions is abnormal!

11:14.240 --> 11:19.070
The world went haywire thanks to life 
that prefers warm climates and sunlight!

11:19.070 --> 11:20.370
Um...

11:20.370 --> 11:24.380
In any case, make sure you tear off 
all the bitt—all of <i>that</i>!

11:24.380 --> 11:25.760
Oh, sure.

11:25.760 --> 11:26.980
That was our plan anyw—

11:26.980 --> 11:28.050
How revolting.

11:30.040 --> 11:31.860
She really hates it.

11:31.860 --> 11:34.850
Well, guess we have to pick 
all of these now.

11:34.850 --> 11:36.370
What if it's all part of their plot?

11:36.370 --> 11:38.460
What plot, exactly? Whose?

11:38.460 --> 11:40.970
To prevent us from leaving this place.

11:40.970 --> 11:42.590
Again with your weird delusions.

11:42.590 --> 11:43.500
I'm not delusional!

11:43.750 --> 11:44.550
Akira.

11:44.550 --> 11:46.640
You're on bitter melon pruning duty with me.

11:46.640 --> 11:49.470
Reimi and Nadeko-chan, 
you go shopping in the meantime.

11:49.470 --> 11:50.160
What?!

11:50.160 --> 11:52.780
We need some food that 
won't spoil, don't we?

11:52.780 --> 11:53.950
It's dangerous!

11:53.950 --> 11:54.930
You're right.

11:54.930 --> 11:56.590
I am a bit worried about what we have.

11:56.590 --> 11:57.660
Nadeko-chan!

11:57.660 --> 11:59.650
Does Higashi-Agano have 
any convenience stores?

11:59.650 --> 12:00.460
I can't wait!

12:00.460 --> 12:01.140
Reimi!

12:01.140 --> 12:02.470
Thanks.

12:05.030 --> 12:07.410
Shi... Re... Na...

12:12.330 --> 12:13.690
What's the big idea?!

12:13.690 --> 12:15.410
Bad! Bad idea!

12:15.410 --> 12:16.640
Why's that?

12:16.640 --> 12:18.500
You take the other side, Akira.

12:18.500 --> 12:20.720
I thought we were going to Ikebukuro!

12:20.720 --> 12:21.720
We sure are.

12:21.720 --> 12:23.340
Where's your enthusiasm?!

12:23.340 --> 12:26.350
I don't know how you can be so relaxed!

12:27.840 --> 12:29.820
I'll go check up on them!

12:40.750 --> 12:42.060
What's going on?!

12:42.060 --> 12:43.090
This is bad!

12:53.830 --> 12:56.140
Reimi! Nadeko-chan!

12:56.140 --> 12:58.060
She said we can take these for free.

12:57.080 --> 13:01.590
<b>The Original Nostalgic Flavor</b>

12:57.080 --> 13:01.590
<b>Chicken Noodles</b>

12:57.080 --> 13:01.590
<b>For Emergency Supplies</b>

12:57.080 --> 13:01.590
<b>Long-Life Hardtack</b>

12:57.080 --> 13:01.590
<b>Always Safe & Refreshing</b>

12:57.080 --> 13:01.590
<b>Emergency Drinking Water</b>

12:58.060 --> 12:59.850
Are you really sure?

12:59.850 --> 13:02.160
We don't need them anymore.

13:02.160 --> 13:02.840
Anymore?

13:04.120 --> 13:07.590
Y-You girls need them more than we do.

13:07.590 --> 13:09.730
So generous of you!

13:09.730 --> 13:12.330
This should be more than enough 
for the time being.

13:12.330 --> 13:15.200
You know we can't repay 
any of your kindness.

13:15.200 --> 13:16.960
We're about to head out soon.

13:16.960 --> 13:20.300
People in Higashi-Agano 
are nice, unlike Agano.

13:20.300 --> 13:21.440
Not to mention serene.

13:21.440 --> 13:23.100
They're benevolent folks at heart.

13:23.100 --> 13:25.290
That's not true at all.

13:25.290 --> 13:31.440
Higashi-Agano had its fair share of 
worried and discontented humans.

13:31.440 --> 13:34.360
But, you see, we came to a realization 
after the 7G incident.

13:34.820 --> 13:38.030
Instead of a miserable life 
filled with suffering,

13:38.030 --> 13:42.320
it's better to live a short, 
satisfying life to its fullest.

13:43.450 --> 13:47.620
Once I came to terms with that, 
all of my anger subsided.

13:47.970 --> 13:50.680
That's so deep, Matsuta-san.

13:50.680 --> 13:53.880
Do you think we can learn 
to think that way, too?

13:53.880 --> 13:55.920
Yes, I know you can.

13:55.920 --> 13:58.360
It won't be long for you all.

13:59.700 --> 14:00.340
Hey!

14:00.340 --> 14:01.820
Let's get going already!

14:01.820 --> 14:03.740
Shizuru-chan was worried about you.

14:03.740 --> 14:05.780
Worried? Why?

14:05.780 --> 14:08.560
I wish I could be like Matsuta-san.

14:08.560 --> 14:10.890
No! We're going to Ikebukuro!

14:10.890 --> 14:12.640
What? Ikebukuro?

14:12.640 --> 14:14.260
Can't we stay in Higashi-Agano?

14:14.260 --> 14:15.240
That sounds nice.

14:15.240 --> 14:16.400
We can't do that!

14:16.400 --> 14:18.890
We need to go find Yoka-chan!

14:22.210 --> 14:23.490
Shizuru-chan?

14:23.490 --> 14:24.670
You didn't prune the bitter melon.

14:24.670 --> 14:26.100
Bitter melon?

14:26.100 --> 14:27.500
Right, the bitter melon.

14:27.850 --> 14:31.130
I started feeling like there wasn't 
any point to any of this.

14:31.130 --> 14:31.860
What?!

14:31.860 --> 14:34.800
Can we really make it to Ikebukuro?

14:34.800 --> 14:36.870
I don't think we can.

14:36.870 --> 14:38.030
You're kidding me!

14:38.030 --> 14:39.870
We only just set out yesterday!

14:39.870 --> 14:43.410
Even if we get there, it's not 
going to make any difference.

14:43.410 --> 14:45.890
I thought you wanted to find Yoka-chan!

14:45.890 --> 14:49.800
Even if we find her, 
it might not change anything.

14:49.800 --> 14:52.960
Heck, she might not even want to see us.

14:52.960 --> 14:55.210
You don't know that unless you find her!

14:55.210 --> 14:55.990
Hey!

14:55.990 --> 14:57.990
Reimi, Nadeko-chan, back me up here!

14:57.990 --> 14:59.010
I'm sleepy.

15:01.870 --> 15:04.080
Pipe down, Akira.

15:04.080 --> 15:07.120
Who wants to stay alive 
if it's miserable and awful?

15:07.120 --> 15:10.450
You can't beat a short, 
happy, and easy life.

15:12.170 --> 15:14.490
Damn it! They're goners!

15:14.980 --> 15:15.890
Five o'clock!

15:19.200 --> 15:21.990
<i>Akira here. Now in Higashi-Agano.</i>

15:23.260 --> 15:25.930
<i>Agano here. Report your situation.</i>

15:26.360 --> 15:27.710
<i>Lots of mushrooms.</i>

15:27.710 --> 15:28.870
<i>Too many mushrooms.</i>

15:28.490 --> 15:30.450
<b>Agano Station</b>

15:28.870 --> 15:30.450
<i>Tell me risk level of mushrooms.</i>

15:30.900 --> 15:32.710
<i>What? Mushrooms?</i>

15:32.710 --> 15:33.400
<i>Leave it to me!</i>

15:33.400 --> 15:36.250
<i>"Matsutake for scent, shimeji for flavor"?</i>

15:36.250 --> 15:38.550
<i>"Use dogs, not pigs, for truffles"?</i>

15:38.550 --> 15:39.870
<i>"Black preferred over white"?</i>

15:40.220 --> 15:44.510
<i>Mushrooms sometimes grow 
in a circular, ring-like shape.</i>

15:44.510 --> 15:47.630
<i>This was believed to be the work 
of fairies or witches in olden times.</i>

15:47.630 --> 15:51.300
<i>In fact, this happens due to 
fungal growth and death cycles.</i>

15:51.300 --> 15:54.980
<i>They also say mushrooms grow 
where lightning has struck, but...</i>

15:54.980 --> 15:56.890
<i>I don't care about lightning!</i>

15:56.890 --> 15:59.380
<i>How do you avoid and escape mushrooms?!</i>

15:59.380 --> 16:01.880
<i>"Mushrooms like moist, dark choo-choo..."</i>

16:01.880 --> 16:03.890
<i>"Choo choo-choo, choo choo-choo..."</i>

16:07.440 --> 16:10.290
We wasted our precious five minutes 
on dumb mushroom trivia!

16:20.800 --> 16:21.770
Bitter melon!

16:23.510 --> 16:24.880
Go away!

16:27.860 --> 16:29.580
Why fight back?

16:29.580 --> 16:31.600
Just join us.

16:31.600 --> 16:32.590
Shut up!

16:32.590 --> 16:35.140
What do you gain from living like this?

16:35.140 --> 16:37.810
I'd gain even less from 
turning into a mushroom!

16:37.810 --> 16:38.830
It's okay.

16:38.830 --> 16:40.260
Mushrooms don't worry.

16:40.260 --> 16:41.800
Mushrooms don't suffer.

16:41.800 --> 16:43.640
Mushrooms don't think.

16:43.990 --> 16:46.360
Let's all become mushrooms.

16:46.360 --> 16:47.440
No way in hell!

16:47.740 --> 16:49.150
It's fun.

16:53.780 --> 16:54.650
Mushrooms!

16:54.650 --> 16:55.810
Army of mushrooms!

17:00.570 --> 17:02.920
Be quiet, Akira.

17:02.920 --> 17:04.700
I want a peaceful life.

17:04.700 --> 17:08.080
No thoughts, just drifting along.

17:08.080 --> 17:09.660
Snap out of it!

17:09.660 --> 17:12.140
What was all that talk 
about going to Ikebukuro?!

17:12.140 --> 17:13.100
Ikebukuro...

17:13.100 --> 17:16.130
Didn't you want to go to Ikebukuro 
and act all trendy?!

17:16.130 --> 17:17.260
Trendy?

17:17.260 --> 17:19.380
What happened to finding Yoka?!

17:20.650 --> 17:21.850
Yoka...

17:21.850 --> 17:25.790
Do you really want to stay here 
growing mushrooms?!

17:26.750 --> 17:27.780
Yoka.

17:30.400 --> 17:35.690
Yoka left Agano and disappeared on us 
without a word.

17:35.690 --> 17:37.210
Who cares about her?

17:37.210 --> 17:38.380
That's not right!

17:38.380 --> 17:39.820
She's our friend!

17:39.820 --> 17:41.550
Friend...

17:41.550 --> 17:43.530
Was she really our friend?

17:43.830 --> 17:46.810
She wouldn't have left us
if she was a friend.

17:46.810 --> 17:52.710
And it's not like I understood 
how Yoka felt at all.

17:53.910 --> 17:57.050
Shizuru, you have so much 
to gain by studying.

17:57.050 --> 17:59.640
What? I'm fine losing.

18:00.990 --> 18:04.400
You haven't handed in your future 
career form yet, have you?

18:04.400 --> 18:05.960
Career, huh?

18:05.960 --> 18:07.530
Do you know what you want to be?

18:07.530 --> 18:08.470
I sure do.

18:08.470 --> 18:10.010
I want to be really smart!

18:10.010 --> 18:12.020
You'll need to study for that.

18:12.020 --> 18:13.370
Again with the studying?

18:15.730 --> 18:17.050
Do you know, Yoka?

18:17.050 --> 18:17.730
I do.

18:17.730 --> 18:19.170
What? What is it?

18:19.170 --> 18:20.500
I want to go to Ikebukuro.

18:20.500 --> 18:21.650
Don't play dumb!

18:21.650 --> 18:23.910
You can do that by taking one train!

18:23.910 --> 18:27.590
Maybe I should become an MMA fighter 
with my Agano jiu-jitsu.

18:27.590 --> 18:29.690
I want to fight an anteater.

18:29.690 --> 18:30.820
Sounds good to me.

18:30.820 --> 18:32.310
Take this seriously!

18:32.310 --> 18:33.930
I'm being serious.

18:34.680 --> 18:35.830
Yoka...

18:35.830 --> 18:37.000
That's right!

18:37.000 --> 18:39.540
We're going to Ikebukuro to see Yoka-chan!

18:39.540 --> 18:43.320
See Yoka in Ikebukuro.

18:50.060 --> 18:50.950
Yeah!

18:50.250 --> 18:51.100
Don't do it!

18:51.100 --> 18:52.400
You'd give up that peace and quiet?!

18:52.400 --> 18:53.430
Don't be a rebel!

18:54.300 --> 18:59.700
I'll be the one to decide 
whether to live an easy life or not!

19:00.700 --> 19:02.390
Shizuru-chan!

19:06.280 --> 19:06.790
Who're you?

19:08.250 --> 19:09.560
I'm kidding!

19:09.560 --> 19:11.020
Just a clever little joke.

19:11.020 --> 19:12.670
Sheesh!

19:11.840 --> 19:13.170
Sorry, sorry.

19:13.170 --> 19:15.360
Let's yank those mushrooms off 
of Nadeko-chan and Reimi.

19:15.360 --> 19:15.920
Yeah.

19:15.920 --> 19:18.380
Don't you realize how good you have it?!

19:17.120 --> 19:19.150
Protect our new brethren!

19:19.150 --> 19:22.180
They're not yours!

19:25.280 --> 19:26.250
Huh?

19:26.250 --> 19:28.850
What was I doing?

19:29.530 --> 19:31.530
Mushroom! Mushroom!

19:31.800 --> 19:34.290
The mushrooms have taken over their minds!

19:34.290 --> 19:34.980
What do we do?

19:34.980 --> 19:37.660
We can't get away while 
we're surrounded like this.

19:39.090 --> 19:40.440
Bitter melon...

19:40.440 --> 19:41.500
Maybe if I...

19:43.490 --> 19:44.960
Take care of the rest.

19:44.960 --> 19:45.590
What?!

19:45.590 --> 19:46.370
Wait!

19:46.370 --> 19:50.200
Bitter melon!

19:53.350 --> 19:55.670
Stop! Please stop!

19:55.670 --> 19:59.680
Are you happy being fed on 
and controlled by mushrooms?

19:59.680 --> 20:02.910
I told you to stop, damn it!

20:04.240 --> 20:05.170
Um...

20:05.170 --> 20:05.850
Matsuta-san?

20:05.850 --> 20:07.560
Whaddaya want?

20:07.560 --> 20:08.900
For cryin' out loud!

20:08.900 --> 20:10.750
Mind yer own business!

20:10.750 --> 20:12.760
We were tryin' to do you a favor!

20:12.760 --> 20:14.120
A favor?

20:14.120 --> 20:17.050
We <i>chose</i> the path of the mushroom!

20:17.050 --> 20:20.450
To hell with spendin' decades in this 
godforsaken world with no future!

20:20.450 --> 20:23.220
Growing mushrooms, turning into 
happy, hippie homebodies,

20:23.220 --> 20:26.160
and dying in one to two years 
is a way better option!

20:26.160 --> 20:28.240
Dying in one to two years?

20:28.240 --> 20:30.430
What's the point in goin' to Ikebukuro?

20:30.430 --> 20:31.280
It's a waste of time!

20:31.560 --> 20:34.600
I have a friend I want to see again.

20:34.600 --> 20:35.800
And then what?

20:35.800 --> 20:38.150
Hell, I bet ya won't even find her.

20:38.150 --> 20:39.860
I'm still going to go.

20:39.860 --> 20:42.000
I won't be happy until 
I go and see for myself!

20:42.000 --> 20:43.680
Ya damn fool!

20:43.680 --> 20:48.300
I hope ya choke on yer own blood 
and end up miserable and half-dead.

20:48.300 --> 20:49.630
Don't come cryin' to me then.

20:54.130 --> 20:55.140
Let's go.

20:57.490 --> 20:59.600
Have it yer way.

21:03.380 --> 21:04.430
Um...

21:04.430 --> 21:06.670
Thanks for the food.

21:07.820 --> 21:09.500
Whatever.

21:24.710 --> 21:26.420
Mushrooms, huh?

21:26.780 --> 21:28.940
I wonder how it feels.

21:28.940 --> 21:31.080
Reimi-chan, you had some 
growing on you already.

21:31.080 --> 21:32.390
You too, Nadeko-chan.

21:33.770 --> 21:38.020
If they grew bigger, we might 
have been okay dying like that.

21:38.020 --> 21:40.900
Maybe it feels good in its own way.

21:40.900 --> 21:42.290
Just going with the flow.

21:42.290 --> 21:45.370
It was a mysterious feeling... 
or, well, just weird.

21:45.370 --> 21:46.700
Hang on!

21:46.700 --> 21:48.920
You should all be thanking me!

21:48.920 --> 21:49.820
For what?

21:49.820 --> 21:51.310
Saving your butts!

21:51.310 --> 21:52.960
Yeah, yeah, thanks a ton.

21:52.960 --> 21:54.170
Say it like you mean it!

21:54.170 --> 21:55.130
Hey!

21:55.130 --> 21:56.380
Even Pochi-san shows me no respect!

21:57.660 --> 21:58.730
What's wrong?

21:58.730 --> 21:59.970
Nothing!

22:07.220 --> 22:10.010
29 Stops Left Until Ikebukuro
